# <domain> — the domain's half of ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md

Optional. The base's `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` holds the operating standards true on any machine and
imports this file after them. Put here only what is true of this domain: who the user is and what
"good" means here (understanding or throughput), whether usage is a flat subscription or billed, how
commits are signed and what a signing failure looks like, and any further imports (a private tooling
list, a knowledge-base projection) as `@/absolute/path` lines. A file already kept by hand at
`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is saved as `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md.before-base` on the base's first apply; move
its domain-specific parts here.
